  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA n2000 (single profile) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while image-only with ResNet50 is very weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether multiprofile representation with aggregation (avgpool) can improve upon the single-profile RNA baseline, and this is a foundational design choice that gates many downstream configurations. This experiment (config_002) is a minimal, clean extension of config_001—same encoder (PCA n2000), same modality (RNA), only adding multiprofile + avgpool—so it isolates the effect of multiprofile aggregation without confounding encoder or modality changes. If multiprofile helps, it validates a large family of configurations (transformer aggregation, other encoders, multimodal variants); if it doesn't, it efficiently prunes that branch and directs remaining budget toward encoder improvements or image modality exploration. With 7 experiments left, reducing uncertainty on this high-leverage design axis is the best use of the next slot."
}

